> Boundary data: conormal signs at both ends

The API uses the outward conormal p du/dn, with du/dn=−u' on the left and
+u' on the right. Thus a right Neumann value two with a zero left Dirichlet
value gives u=2x. Mirroring the conditions gives u=2(1−x). Physical diffusive
outward flux is −p du/dn, so the API's positive conormal must not be called
positive outward heat flow without changing the sign convention.

For Robin data p du/dn+alpha(u−u_ambient)=0, move the alpha*u term to the
matrix and alpha*u_ambient to the load. The original right Robin condition
alpha=3,u_ambient=4 with zero left value gives u=3x. Its mirror gives
u=3(1−x). Each test retains a Dirichlet constraint, avoiding the constant
nullspace of pure Neumann diffusion. Nonnegative reaction/Robin coefficients
and appropriate constraints are relevant to the coercive stability model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fem_boundaries.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/fem/fem.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/interpolation_extra.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/cubic_spline.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <vector>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto mesh=dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,10);const dm::fem::BoundaryCondition1D zero{},neumann{dm::fem::BCType::Neumann,2,0},robin{dm::fem::BCType::Robin,4,3};auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();std::print("| case | u(0) | u(1) | actual maximum nodal error |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  const std::vector<std::string>names{"Original right Neumann","Original right Robin","Mirror left Neumann","Mirror left Robin"};const std::vector<std::string>legend{"Right Neumann","Right Robin","Left Neumann","Left Robin"};const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB>colours{{37,99,235},{22,163,74},{220,38,38},{124,58,237}};
  for(int which=0;which<4;++which){const bool mirror=which>=2;const double slope=which%2?3:2;const auto natural=which%2?robin:neumann;const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(mesh,{1},{0},"zero",{},mirror?natural:zero,mirror?zero:natural);const auto e=dm::algorithms::interpolation_error_scan([&](double x){return dm::algorithms::linear_interpolate(r.nodes,r.u,x);},[=](double x){return slope*(mirror?1-x:x);},r.nodes);std::print("| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.10e} |\n",names[which],r.u.front(),r.u.back(),e.max_abs_error);plot.line(r.nodes,r.u,legend[which],colours[which],2).points(r.nodes,r.u,"",colours[which],3);if(e.max_abs_error>1e-12)throw std::runtime_error("linear boundary check failed");}
  plot.title("Original and mirrored outward-conormal boundary checks").x_label("x").y_label("Actual nodal u").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/fem_boundaries.svg");
}
