> Transient heat: reuse one actual history

Spatial Galerkin discretization gives M U_dot+K U=F, where M is the unit
mass matrix for the time derivative, distinct from the reaction contribution
inside K. Backward Euler on an actual positive time interval delta_t gives

\[
(M/\Delta t+K)U^{n+1}=MU^n/\Delta t+F.
\]

The named-source transient API uses the same source constructor as the steady
API and delegates to the same actual time loop as the live-source entry point.
No report-local source subclass or second time integrator is required. The
source and boundary data describe a fixed spatial model; the live callback
is reevaluated during quadrature on every time advance.

The original model uses twenty elements, p=1,q=0.5, source one, zero endpoint
and initial values, and nominal dt=0.02 through t=5. One actual full history
supplies the original four end-time checks and the plotted slices. Each
comparison uses the matching discrete steady solution, so this is a relaxation
check, not a continuum time-discretization error measurement.

For a coercive semidiscrete problem, the homogeneous error modes have
amplification 1/(1+lambda*delta_t), with positive generalized eigenvalues
K v=lambda M v. This gives backward Euler's unrestricted-step stability for
that model. It does not guarantee accuracy for large steps, nor remove finite
arithmetic or linear-solver limitations. Forward Euler instead needs
|1−lambda*delta_t|≤1, so its actual bound depends on the largest eigenvalue;
h² is a scaling guide rather than a universal numerical step threshold.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fem_transient.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/fem/fem.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/interpolation_extra.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/cubic_spline.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <vector>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto mesh=dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,20);const auto steady=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(mesh,{1},{.5},"constant",{1},{},{});const auto history=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(mesh,{1},{.5},"constant",{1},{},{},std::vector<double>(21,0),5,.02);std::vector<double>times,gaps;auto profiles=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for(std::size_t j=0;j<history.times.size();++j){const auto e=dm::algorithms::interpolation_error_scan([&](double x){return dm::algorithms::linear_interpolate(history.nodes,history.u[j],x);},[&](double x){return dm::algorithms::linear_interpolate(steady.nodes,steady.u,x);},history.nodes);times.push_back(history.times[j]);gaps.push_back(std::log10(std::max(e.max_abs_error,1e-16)));}
  std::print("| original end time | actual stored time | actual maximum nodal gap to discrete steady state |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");for(double time:{.5,1.,2.,5.}){const auto it=std::find(history.times.begin(),history.times.end(),time);if(it==history.times.end())throw std::runtime_error("original time absent");const auto j=static_cast<std::size_t>(it-history.times.begin());double worst=0;for(std::size_t i=0;i<steady.size();++i)worst=std::max(worst,std::abs(history.u[j][i]-steady.u[i]));std::print("| {:.1f} | {:.17g} | {:.10e} |\n",time,history.times[j],worst);}
  const std::vector<double>selected{.2,.5,1,5};const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB>colours{{220,38,38},{251,146,60},{14,165,233},{37,99,235}};for(std::size_t k=0;k<selected.size();++k){const auto it=std::find(history.times.begin(),history.times.end(),selected[k]);if(it==history.times.end())throw std::runtime_error("slice time absent");const auto j=static_cast<std::size_t>(it-history.times.begin());profiles.line(history.nodes,history.u[j],std::format("t={}",selected[k]),colours[k],2);}profiles.title("Original stored time slices").x_label("x").y_label("Actual nodal u(x,t)");auto relaxation=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();relaxation.line(times,gaps,"Actual nodal gap",{124,58,237},2).title("Gap to matching discrete steady state").x_label("Actual time").y_label("log10 max(gap, 1e-16)");std::print("\nTransient history: nodes {}; stored frames {}; actual advances {}; final time {}.\n",history.num_nodes(),history.num_steps(),history.num_steps()-1,history.times.back());dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(profiles).add(relaxation).size(1100,550).title("Original backward-Euler relaxation from one actual history").fit_panels().save_svg("build/fem_transient.svg");
}
