> Preserve the triangular two-dimensional examples

For −k Delta u=f, linear basis functions on each triangle have constant
gradients. Their stiffness contribution is k*area*(grad phi_i dot grad phi_j).
The native mesh uses counterclockwise triangles, and the solver applies
Dirichlet elimination before its sparse conjugate-gradient solve.

The three edge-midpoint load rule is exact through degree two of the integrand;
therefore it integrates linear spatial sources times P1 test functions exactly.
It is not an exact rule for arbitrary quadratic source terms times those tests.
The sine load below uses numerical quadrature. The selected cases measure
actual errors; the public basic result does not expose a CG convergence status
or an independently certified algebraic residual.

We retain the original 6-by-6 harmonic linear test u=x+2y and the original
8,16,32 cell-per-side Poisson refinements with exact solution sin(pi x)sin(pi y).
The table's maximum is over mesh nodes. A sampled nodal rate near two on this
structured sequence does not establish a general max-norm theorem on arbitrary
meshes. The final y=0.5 slice is extracted from the actual finest result.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fem_triangles.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/fem/fem.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/interpolation_extra.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/cubic_spline.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <vector>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const double pi=3.14159265358979323846;auto linear_mesh=dm::fem::make_rectangular_mesh2d(0,0,1,1,6,6);auto boundary=dm::fem::boundary_nodes(linear_mesh);std::vector<double>values;for(int index:boundary){const auto p=linear_mesh.nodes[static_cast<std::size_t>(index)];values.push_back(p.x+2*p.y);}const auto harmonic=dm::fem::FEM2D::solve_builtin(linear_mesh,1,"zero",{},boundary,values);double linear_error=0;for(std::size_t i=0;i<harmonic.size();++i)linear_error=std::max(linear_error,std::abs(harmonic.u[i]-(harmonic.nodes[i].x+2*harmonic.nodes[i].y)));std::print("Original 6x6 harmonic case: nodes {}; maximum nodal error {:.10e}.\n",harmonic.size(),linear_error);if(linear_error>1e-11)throw std::runtime_error("harmonic test failed");
  std::vector<double>lh,le,guide;double previous=0,first=0;dm::fem::FEM2DResult finest;std::print("\n| original cells per side | nodes | actual maximum nodal error | observed order |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");for(std::size_t n:{8,16,32}){const auto mesh=dm::fem::make_rectangular_mesh2d(0,0,1,1,n,n);const auto edges=dm::fem::boundary_nodes(mesh);auto r=dm::fem::FEM2D::solve_builtin(mesh,1,"sine",{2*pi*pi,pi,pi},edges,std::vector<double>(edges.size(),0));double worst=0;for(std::size_t i=0;i<r.size();++i)worst=std::max(worst,std::abs(r.u[i]-std::sin(pi*r.nodes[i].x)*std::sin(pi*r.nodes[i].y)));std::print("| {} | {} | {:.10e} | {} |\n",n,r.size(),worst,previous?std::format("{:.6f}",std::log2(previous/worst)):"initial");if(!first)first=worst;lh.push_back(std::log10(1./n));le.push_back(std::log10(worst));guide.push_back(std::log10(first*std::pow(8./n,2)));previous=worst;finest=std::move(r);}
  auto convergence=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();convergence.line(lh,le,"Measured error",{124,58,237},2).points(lh,le,"",{124,58,237},4).line(lh,guide,"Slope 2 guide",{148,163,184},1.5).title("Original 2D Poisson refinement").x_label("log10 h").y_label("log10 nodal error");std::vector<double>x,computed,reference;for(std::size_t i=0;i<=32;++i){const auto index=16*33+i;const auto p=finest.nodes[index];if(p.y!=.5)throw std::runtime_error("slice row mismatch");x.push_back(p.x);computed.push_back(finest.u[index]);reference.push_back(std::sin(pi*p.x)*std::sin(pi*p.y));}auto slice=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();slice.line(x,reference,"Exact",{37,99,235},2).points(x,computed,"Actual FEM nodes",{220,38,38},3).title("Finest actual y=0.5 cross-section").x_label("x").y_label("u(x,0.5)");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(convergence).add(slice).size(1100,550).title("Original triangular harmonic and manufactured Poisson checks").fit_panels().save_svg("build/fem_triangles.svg");
}
