\caption(Every original triangular mesh executes. The actual finest slice is shown with nodal markers, and the convergence panel compares measured nodal errors with a normalized slope-two guide.)
\alttext(Two native panels show the actual three-mesh two-dimensional Poisson nodal convergence and exact-versus-computed values along the finest mesh row at y equals one half.)

> Actual time levels, named sources and output limits

The former time loop used ceil(t_end/dt) as an unconditional advance count.
For t_end=0.30000000000000004 and dt=0.1, a rounded product already reaches
that end at step three. The old fourth iteration repeated the time, making
its actual interval zero and its final solution nonfinite. The corrected core
stops once the endpoint is reached and rejects any nonadvancing rounded time
before assembly. Its planned final step uses t_end directly, avoiding an
unnecessary overflowing nominal product for very large finite time controls.

Time controls are positive and finite. Frame/container/solution-value counts
are checked before output allocation or source evaluations. Spatial geometry,
finite coefficient/source arithmetic and nonzero Thomas pivots remain caller
preconditions; the basic solver does not certify them for arbitrary edited
meshes or coefficients. Returned output owns its nodes, times and rows. It
stores the full history rather than an optional trace: for S actual advances
and N nodes, it holds N coordinates, S+1 times and N(S+1) solution scalars,
excluding capacities/allocator bytes and assembly temporaries. No optional
history quota is imposed; choosing a large output still has a real memory cost.

The final program checks the corrected time edge, all five named source
families, a shortened interval, rejected controls and a copied result's
independence from later edits. It also compares a single-interior-node decay
with the closed backward-Euler mode 1/(1+12*dt), an independently derived
small-system reference rather than another finite-element implementation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fem_time_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/fem/fem.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/interpolation_extra.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/cubic_spline.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <vector>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto mesh=dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2);auto history=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(mesh,{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{},{0,0,0},.30000000000000004,.1);std::print("| actual frame | actual time | actual interval | midpoint value | finite |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");for(std::size_t j=0;j<history.times.size();++j){const double interval=j?history.times[j]-history.times[j-1]:0;std::print("| {} | {:.17g} | {:.17g} | {:.10f} | {} |\n",j,history.times[j],interval,history.u[j][1],std::isfinite(history.u[j][1]));if(j&&!(interval>0))throw std::runtime_error("duplicate actual time");}std::print("\nCorrected rounded-end case: frames {}; advances {}; final finite {}.\n",history.num_steps(),history.num_steps()-1,std::isfinite(history.u.back()[1]));
  std::print("\n| named spatial source | midpoint after one dt=0.1 step |\n| :--- | ---: |\n");const std::vector<std::string>names{"zero","constant","linear","polynomial","sine"};const std::vector<std::vector<double>>params{{},{1},{1,0},{0,0,1},{1,3.14159265358979323846,0}};for(std::size_t i=0;i<names.size();++i){const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(mesh,{1},{0},names[i],params[i],{},{},{0,0,0},.1,.1);std::print("| {} | {:.10f} |\n",names[i],r.u.back()[1]);}
  const auto decay=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(mesh,{1},{0},"zero",{},{},{},{0,1,0},.5,.5);std::print("\nOne-interior decay: actual {:.12f}; independent backward-Euler value {:.12f}.\n",decay.u.back()[1],1./7);if(std::abs(decay.u.back()[1]-1./7)>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("modal decay check failed");const auto partial=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(mesh,{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{},{0,0,0},.25,.1);std::print("Partial-step history: frames {}; final time {}; last interval {:.17g}.\n",partial.num_steps(),partial.times.back(),partial.times.back()-partial.times[partial.times.size()-2]);auto copy=history;history.u.back()[1]=99;std::print("Owned copy retains finite midpoint {}; edited original midpoint {}.\n",std::isfinite(copy.u.back()[1]),history.u.back()[1]);
  int rejected=0;try{(void)dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(mesh,{1},{0},"missing",{},{},{},{0,0,0},.1,.1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}try{(void)dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(mesh,{1},{0},"zero",{},{},{},{0,0,0},.1,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN());}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}try{(void)dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(mesh,{1},{0},"zero",{},{},{},{0,0,0},1,1e-20);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}std::print("Unknown-source/nonfinite-time/unrepresentable-frame rejections {}/3.\n",rejected);if(rejected!=3||copy.num_steps()!=4||!std::isfinite(copy.u.back()[1]))throw std::runtime_error("time controls failed");
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(58,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=3.5;box.height=1.7;box.font_size=22;for(std::size_t j=0;j<copy.times.size();++j){box.fill=j==0?dm::graphics::RGB{226,232,240}:j+1==copy.times.size()?dm::graphics::RGB{187,247,208}:dm::graphics::RGB{191,219,254};g.node(std::to_string(j),{5.*j,0},std::format("t={:.6f}\nu(mid)={:.6f}",copy.times[j],copy.u[j][1]),box);if(j)g.edge(std::to_string(j-1),std::to_string(j),std::format("dt={:.6g}",copy.times[j]-copy.times[j-1]));}g.text({7.5,3},"Actual time levels reach the final time once",27).text({7.5,-3},"Three positive actual intervals; no zero-duration final update",24).save_svg("build/fem_time_controls.svg");
}
